{
 "readings": {
  "E1": "calendar: W1 = D26's dates 2014-09-01 -> 2019-01-02 (1,070 sessions); W2 = each book's D17 dates of the EXTENDED published NAV (extended_2026-11-25) from its first date (SCMO_0007: 2019-01-04) to END = 2026-11-20, the earliest last date of the three D03 Master files, MAUc1 and the index prices (asserted equal to the pinned end); rows after END are never used",
  "E2": "decision dates = T0 and the last session of every later ISO week; the decision at the last session is made and not traded (T14 E2)",
  "E3": "label = latest Master row dated <= decision date, per index and for MAUc1 (W1: D03 2026-10-30 files and D24b, W2: D03 2026-11-20 files and D24c); regime IN / OUT-BUY / OUT-SELL from the three SIGNs and g; B = the indices whose own SIGN is BUY, k = |B| (used by -idx; -all ignores it); the Smallcap 100 rows are sliced to >= 2011-11-25",
  "E4": "targets per rule from T16.md 2.1: absolute shares (parent e, GOLDBEES, cash, one per index); the six T14 rules map (e, gw) to e, (1-e)gw, (1-e)(1-gw), 0 so their path is T14's; -idx in OUT-SELL = cash and each index of B at 1/(k+1) (T15); -all in OUT-SELL = cash 0.25 and each of the three indices 0.25; one function `rule_targets` serves every run",
  "E5": "initial position at T0's close, no cost: the target of the decision at T0 (IN: the basket in force, drifted from its availableDate, scaled to NAV 1; OUT: the sleeve; e = 0.5: half the drifted basket and half GOLDBEES; -idx in OUT-SELL: cash and each index of B at its T0 close; -all in OUT-SELL: cash and each index at 0.25 of NAV)",
  "E6": "stock fill = OHLC4 of the Eikon bar (close if open/high/low is blank; the last close if no bar); GOLDBEES fill = T03's de-spike with the MCX range of the window's file (W1: D24b daily, W2: D12), raw OHLC4 where the range is missing; index fill = OHLC4 of the index's own bar (D25 in W1, D25d in W2); an index trade on a session without a bar stops the run",
  "E7": "costs: T14's `trade` generalised to index lines (cost = ow x value traded over every line, stocks, GOLDBEES, cash and each index, then every target scaled by (V-cost)/V)",
  "E8": "a basket takes effect on the first session on or after its availableDate; skipped baskets dropped; weights renormalised. While e = 1 a basket change is the full reset trade; while 0 < e < 1 (the -half comparators) it is T14's D1 partial trade; while e = 0 (-idx and -all in OUT-SELL included) nothing is traded",
  "E9": "trade kinds: switch_in / switch_out (e crosses 0 or 1 between IN and OUT-BUY; for -orig also IN <-> OUT-SELL), sleeve_rebalance, regime_in / regime_out (into / out of OUT-SELL, rules other than -orig), index_set_change (-idx: B changed while OUT-SELL on both sides; never for -all), basket_change",
  "E10": "cash level: W1 the extended LBES 2026-11-05 (D11), W2 the extended LBES 2026-11-25, as-of on sessions; R2 'liq': W1 liquidEtfFinal (LIQUIDCASE) over the whole window, W2 LBES to the session before 2024-01-24 then LIQUIDCASE returns; no accrual",
  "E11": "constant mix at each rule's own average shares: parent f_p = mean of e over the weekly decisions, GOLDBEES f_g, cash f_c and each index f_i = the means of the rule's target shares; rebalanced at every decision date's next session and at every basket change while f_p > 0 (T14 E11 generalised); initial stock holding = drifted basket scaled by f_p",
  "E12": "R3: W1 starts at the first D26 session on or after 2015-01-02, W2 'live' at the first D17 session on or after 2021-11-01, each with its own first state (both start in OUT-SELL, so -idx starts holding cash and the indices of B at their closes and -all holds 25% of each of cash and the three indices)",
  "E13": "ledger span (T16.md 2.4, 'first fill to last fill'): a = the session on which the first decision of the span is traded (the session after it; T0 for the window's first decision), b = the session on which the decision that ends the span is traded (or the last session); returns are close[b] / close[a] - 1 of each instrument and of each rule's 20.8 bps NAV (parent = hold-parent 0-cost NAV); rows carry all_minus_idx_<base> = ret(b-all) - ret(b-idx) so the k = 0 and k >= 1 stretches can be summed apart",
  "E14": "R4: for each OUT-SELL spell s, -all runs with target = cash 1 (-liq's) on the decisions of spell s only; every other week is the real rule; 20.8 bps, full window, LBES",
  "E15": "R5: every index's OHLC4 and close of session i (i = 0 at T0 on the book's calendar) multiplied by (1 - 0.005 / 252)^i, for -idx, -all and every other rule (the others hold no index); 20.8 bps",
  "E16": "index bars: a calendar session with no bar carries the last close (marking only); counted per index; a trade that involves an index line on such a session stops the run",
  "E18": "comparator eq3_index_basket: one third each of Nifty 100, Midcap 100 and Smallcap 100, no cash and no parent, rebalanced at every weekly decision's next session (as the constant mixes), 20.8 bps, initial position free at T0's close",
  "E17": "V4(a) boundary: W2's eight T15 rules are compared with T15's stored NAVs and trades only on sessions and trade dates <= 2026-10-30 (T15's last W2 decision, 2026-10-30, was not traded; here it is, on the next session, so later rows are new); W1 is compared on every session"
 },
